\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1.6}{\ignorespaces Simplified schematic of the current (left) and of the new (right) CSC electronics for the inner rings formed by ME2/1, ME3/1 and ME4/1. The orange lines mark optical data transfer, the blue lines represent copper cables.. \relax }}{7}{figure.caption.20}}
\newlabel{Fig:dcfeb}{{1.6}{7}{Simplified schematic of the current (left) and of the new (right) CSC electronics for the inner rings formed by ME2/1, ME3/1 and ME4/1. The orange lines mark optical data transfer, the blue lines represent copper cables.. \relax }{figure.caption.20}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1.1}{\ignorespaces  Summary of the CSC electronics boards that will be upgraded during LS2 and LS3. Boards above the horizontal line are placed on-chamber, while those below the line occur in off-chamber crates. Of the 540 new DCFEBv2s, 504 will be installed in the ME1/1 chambers, while the rest plus the DCFEBs currently in ME1/1 will be installed in ME2/1. The ALCTs in stations 2, 3, and 4 will be upgraded during LS2 while those in station 1 will be upgraded in LS3. The ALCTs in ME1/3 do not need upgrading because they will be replaced with the ALCT-S6 currently installed in ME1/1. \relax }}{8}{table.caption.21}}
\newlabel{electronics_upgrades}{{1.1}{8}{Summary of the CSC electronics boards that will be upgraded during LS2 and LS3. Boards above the horizontal line are placed on-chamber, while those below the line occur in off-chamber crates. Of the 540 new DCFEBv2s, 504 will be installed in the ME1/1 chambers, while the rest plus the DCFEBs currently in ME1/1 will be installed in ME2/1. The ALCTs in stations 2, 3, and 4 will be upgraded during LS2 while those in station 1 will be upgraded in LS3. The ALCTs in ME1/3 do not need upgrading because they will be replaced with the ALCT-S6 currently installed in ME1/1. \relax }{table.caption.21}{}}
